PATCH 200: the DCBS unit-database chunk handler chain (b21d/b1a2/d81e/43c1) -- DGROUP
near-offset-as-host-pointer base-losses + the dropped DI record-slot thread.

Exposed once patch 199 let FUN_0000_d501 parse past SHDR: the very first DCBS ("Deployment"
unit database) record dispatched d7e1 -> d81e -> b1a2 -> b21d, which SIGSEGV'd because the whole
DCBS record chain is hand-asm that threads the object/slot pointer through DS-relative near-offsets
and the DI register -- all base-lost by Ghidra (near-offset used as a host pointer -> wild deref).

ASM-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00):
 - FUN_1000_b21d (0x1b21d): the roster INSERT.  bx=ax=obj near-offset; registers it in the friendly
   roster (slot table DGROUP:0xa022 stride 0x37, presence flags DAT_2000_a2f7[]) or enemy roster
   (0xc05c stride 0xfb, flags DAT_2000_a38d[]) per the team bit byte[obj-0x19ec]&1; stores obj at
   word[di], slot index at word[di+2]; returns the slot near-offset in DI and CF (full at 0x96).
   Ghidra base-lost byte[obj-0x19ec] and the slot pointer (`(int*)0xa022` host deref -> SIGSEGV),
   typed the slot stores int(4B) at [di]/[di+4] not WORD at [di]/[di+2], and dropped the DI output.
 - FUN_1000_b1a2 (0x1b1a2): calls b21d(obj) -> di; publishes {di, cx} into the DGROUP:0x9fbc/0x9fbe
   index tables at word[idx*2]; zeroes the slot body (0x33 friendly / 0xf7 enemy).  Threads b21d's
   DI as its own return; base-lost DS accesses rebased.
 - FUN_0000_d81e (0xd81e): allocates the slot via b1a2 -> di, saves word[di+2], reads the record
   body (a9c2-2 bytes) into DS:(di+2), restores [di+2], processes via 43c1(di).  DI (Ghidra
   unaff_CS) rebased.
 - FUN_0000_43c1 (0x43c1): the unit-record installer -- sets type/state flags [di+0x16]/[di+0x17],
   registers di in the cell-index table DGROUP:0x6d3c (=&DAT_2000_2d3c), runs c296.  di rebased and
   the param_1[N] word indexes (uint*=N*4) corrected to the 2-byte asm stride.

VERIFIED (shim AZER1.FSG handle trace, FIST_CASCADE 3-click route): the FSG parse now runs to
COMPLETION -- 268 handle-8 reads through the whole DCBS record set (record bodies 249B enemy / 53B
friendly, matching the 0xfb/0x37 slot strides), then PATH/STMP/PINF/BINF/TERM -> d501 returns
normally (finalize path, a974 set by the TERM handler).  Execution advances off the parser entirely
into the model-load path e006->42cc->4308, where the next frontier is the model-element enter-dirty
mark FUN_1000_8daa (the FUN_1000_8390/842d base-loss class -- a separate subsystem, held).
Behaviour-neutral for the 19 covered flows: b21d/b1a2/d81e/43c1 run only inside the mission FSG
DCBS parse, off the menu/dialog paths (verify 19/19).
